 "description": "See how the declared authentication surface changed between two OpenAPI documents. Reports schemes added, removed or altered, scopes gained or lost, and the two cases a scheme comparison alone misses: an operation that now requires authentication where it required none, and an operation that no longer requires any. Reports what the documents say, not what the implementation enforces. Pay 120000 atomic USDC on Base via exact x402. MCP does not pay; it provides a challenge handoff.",
 "inputSchema": {
  "additionalProperties": false,
  "properties": {
   "after": {
    "description": "An OpenAPI 3.x document as JSON. YAML is not accepted: a YAML reader is a parser dependency and a parser is an attack surface, so convert locally first. $ref resolves inside the document only and a remote reference is reported unresolved, never fetched. Swagger 2 documents are read only as far as they share OpenAPI 3 structure, and the difference is reported.",
    "example": {
     "components": {
      "schemas": {
       "Order": {
        "properties": {
         "id": {
          "type": "string"
         },
         "legacy_ref": {
          "type": "string"
         },
